  "body": "**Blocked by:** #95\n\n## Context\n\nMailbox navigation and reading require a dedicated registered view while still consuming generic database operations.\n\n## Task\n\nRegister `mailbox-client` as a view type and implement a folder/label sidebar with unread counts, message list, and reading pane. On narrow layouts and iOS-sized viewports, show one pane at a time with an explicit back action. Filter through the Emails-to-Folders relation and use generic query/item operations; do not add a mailbox-only read data path. Follow the existing client tokens, i18n, loading, empty, and error conventions.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Registered view, responsive pane state, folder selection, list selection, reading display, and unread counts.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Triage shortcuts, compose/reply, sending logic, and copying Roundcube code.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The view resolves through the registered view mechanism.\n- Desktop shows three panes; narrow layout provides navigable single-pane behavior.\n- Folder filtering and message loading use generic operations.\n- Loading, empty, unavailable, and retryable-error states are tested.\n",
